        "original_id": "0b3b430c-5792-5c01-add6-878ac8c74133",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: International Grenfell Association\n- People: Sir Wilfred Grenfell\n- Places: Newfoundland, Labrador, Battle Harbour, Mary's Harbour\n- Topics: health care, education, religious services, rehabilitation, hospital relocation, fire\n\nFacts:\n- Sir Wilfred Thomason Grenfell was born on 28 February 1865 and died on 9 October 1940.\n- Sir Wilfred Thomason Grenfell was a medical missionary to Newfoundland and Labrador.\n- Sir Wilfred Grenfell founded the International Grenfell Association.\n- The International Grenfell Association provided health care, education, religious services, rehabilitation, and other social activities to fishing and coastal communities in northern Newfoundland and along the coast of Labrador.\n- After a fire destroyed its hospital and boarding school in Battle Harbour, the International Grenfell Association decided to relocate those facilities to Mary's Harbour.",
